    <bpmn:process id="W_W5418" name="W5418. OT Security Architecture, Purdue-Model Zone Design &amp; IT/OT Segmentation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Program stand-up; new site/remodel network design (VS-109); new connected-device channel; recurring architecture review
Frequency: Architecture refresh annual; per major site project
Volume: 1 reference OT architecture + per-site zone design across ~205 sites
Owner: OT Security Architect (Enterprise Architecture, VS-113)
Participants: Network Engineering (VS-27.2), IFM (VS-138), DC Ops (VS-04), HSE (VS-24)
Source: workflow W5418 — OT Security Architecture, Purdue-Model Zone Design &amp; IT/OT Segmentation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5418_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5418_Lane1" name="OT Security Architect">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5418_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5418_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5418_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5418_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5418_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5418_Lane2" name="Network Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5418_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5418_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5418_Start4" name="Program stand-up; new site/remodel network design (VS-109); new connected-device channel…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5418_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5418_Task5" name="Adopt a Purdue Enterprise Reference Architecture / IEC 62443 zone-and-conduit…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Adopt a Purdue Enterprise Reference Architecture / IEC 62443 zone-and-conduit model adapted for retail: Level 0–3 OT (safety/field/control/operations) vs Level 4–5 IT (corporate/internet), with a demilitarized zone (DMZ) between.
Responsible (R): OT Security Architect
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5418_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5418_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5418_Task6" name="Define zone groupings by safety/operational impact: a fire/life-safety zone, a…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Define zone groupings by safety/operational impact: a fire/life-safety zone, a BMS/HVAC zone, a payment zone (POS/SCO/lockers), an energy zone (solar SCADA/EV), a logistics zone (WMS/RF/weighbridge).
Responsible (R): OT Security Architect
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5418_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5418_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5418_Task7" name="Specify the IT/OT boundary controls: one-way data diodes or read-only…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Specify the IT/OT boundary controls: one-way data diodes or read-only historians where feasible, application-layer proxies in the DMZ, deny-by-default firewall policy between zones.
Responsible (R): Network Engineer
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5418_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5418_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5418_Task8" name="Document allowed conduits (which OT system legitimately talks to which IT/cloud…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Document allowed conduits (which OT system legitimately talks to which IT/cloud system — e.g. BMS→IFM cloud, SCADA→utility) and forbid everything else.
Responsible (R): OT Security Architect
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5418_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5418_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5418_Task9" name="Review at the enterprise-architecture forum (VS-113) and align to the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Review at the enterprise-architecture forum (VS-113) and align to the cloud/integration perimeter.
Responsible (R): OT Security Architect
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5418_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5418_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5418_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5418_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-800 (ensure controlled execution — OT Asset Inventory, Architecture &amp; IT/OT Segmentation Governance (PA-190.1).) | - operational: IT/OT segregation; architecture documentation; deny-by-default firewall policy with documented exception conduits.
Owner: OT Security Architect (Enterprise Architecture, VS-113)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5418_Assoc12" sourceRef="W5418_Annotation11" targetRef="W5418_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5418_Flow13" sourceRef="W5418_Start4" targetRef="W5418_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5418_Flow14" sourceRef="W5418_Task5" targetRef="W5418_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5418_Flow15" sourceRef="W5418_Task6" targetRef="W5418_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5418_Flow16" sourceRef="W5418_Task7" targetRef="W5418_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5418_Flow17" sourceRef="W5418_Task8" targetRef="W5418_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5418_Flow18" sourceRef="W5418_Task9" targetRef="W5418_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W5418_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W5418_plane" bpmnElement="W_W5418">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5418_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5418_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5418_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5418_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5418_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5418_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5418_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5418_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5418_End10_di" bpmnElement="W5418_End10"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5418_Annotation11_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Annotation11"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="86" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W5418_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W5418_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W5418_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W5418_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W5418_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W5418_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W5418_Assoc12_di" bpmnElement="W5418_Assoc12"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5419" name="W5419. OT Identity, Credential &amp; Role-Based Access Control Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Program stand-up; device onboarding (W5421); vendor/staff access provisioning
Frequency: Setup; periodic access recertification quarterly
Volume: ~25,000–40,000 OT endpoints + ~300–500 engineering/vendor accounts
Owner: OT Identity Lead (IT Security, VS-27.3)
Participants: IFM (VS-138), vendor service teams, DC/Store ops, HSE (VS-24)
Source: workflow W5419 — OT Identity, Credential &amp; Role-Based Access Control Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5419_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5419_Lane1" name="OT Identity Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5419_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5419_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5419_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5419_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5419_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5419_Lane2" name="OT Security Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5419_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5419_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5419_Start4" name="Program stand-up; device onboarding (W5421); vendor/staff access provisioning">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5419_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5419_Task5" name="Eliminate shared/default credentials on OT devices — per-device unique creds, a…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Eliminate shared/default credentials on OT devices — per-device unique creds, a privileged-access-management (PAM) vault for the engineering-workstation and admin accounts.
Responsible (R): OT Identity Lead
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5419_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5419_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5419_Task6" name="Define OT RBAC roles (read-only operator, maintenance, engineering…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Define OT RBAC roles (read-only operator, maintenance, engineering, vendor-remote) mapped to the zone model (W5418).
Responsible (R): OT Identity Lead
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5419_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5419_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5419_Task7" name="Enforce MFA on all interactive OT/admin access; require jump-host (bastion) for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Enforce MFA on all interactive OT/admin access; require jump-host (bastion) for any vendor/remote OT session (W5433).
Responsible (R): OT Identity Lead
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5419_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5419_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5419_Task8" name="Quarterly recertify OT access — confirm each engineering/vendor account still…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly recertify OT access — confirm each engineering/vendor account still has a live business need (links to VS-167 vetting and VS-161 TPRM).
Responsible (R): OT Security Analyst
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5419_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5419_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5419_Task9" name="Rotate credentials on vendor/contractor offboarding and on role change; revoke…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Rotate credentials on vendor/contractor offboarding and on role change; revoke standing access in favor of just-in-time.
Responsible (R): OT Identity Lead
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
