    <bpmn:process id="W_W5420" name="W5420. OT Device Hardening, Secure Configuration Baseline &amp; Change Control" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Program stand-up; device onboarding (W5421); vulnerability/findings remediation
Frequency: Baseline refresh annual; per-device hardening at onboarding
Volume: 1 baseline per OT device class (BMS, fire, PLC, SCADA, POS, SCO, locker, EV, RF, weighbridge)
Owner: OT Security Engineer
Participants: IFM (VS-138), DC Ops (VS-04), vendor service, HSE (VS-24), Change Advisory (VS-27.1)
Source: workflow W5420 — OT Device Hardening, Secure Configuration Baseline &amp; Change Control</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5420_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5420_Lane1" name="OT Security Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5420_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5420_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5420_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5420_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5420_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5420_Lane2" name="OT Security Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5420_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5420_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5420_Start4" name="Program stand-up; device onboarding (W5421); vulnerability/findings remediation">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5420_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5420_Task5" name="Author a secure-configuration baseline per OT device class (disable unused…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Author a secure-configuration baseline per OT device class (disable unused services/ports, enforce logging, disable vendor cloud links unless approved, lock engineering-mode).
Responsible (R): OT Security Engineer
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: per class</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5420_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5420_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5420_Task6" name="Validate each baseline against a non-production instance before deployment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Validate each baseline against a non-production instance before deployment (never harden a live safety system untested).
Responsible (R): OT Security Engineer
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: per class</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5420_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5420_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5420_Task7" name="Submit hardening changes through the OT-aware change-control process (VS-27.1)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Submit hardening changes through the OT-aware change-control process (VS-27.1) with explicit safety/ops impact assessment and rollback.
Responsible (R): OT Security Engineer
Accountable (A): Change Advisory Board
Duration: per change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5420_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5420_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5420_Task8" name="Apply the baseline at onboarding (W5421) and on a remediation sweep for in-life…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Apply the baseline at onboarding (W5421) and on a remediation sweep for in-life devices, in a maintenance window with ops standby.
Responsible (R): OT Security Engineer / Vendor
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: per device</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5420_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5420_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5420_Task9" name="Re-baseline when a vendor firmware/PLC revision changes; track config drift…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Re-baseline when a vendor firmware/PLC revision changes; track config drift between audits.
Responsible (R): OT Security Analyst
Accountable (A): OT Security Lead
Duration: ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5420_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5420_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5420_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
